---
// Pearl › 01 — The Setup (Figma 186:2844): label, headline (second half muted) and lead
// paragraph. The headline wraps naturally (user).
import Section from './Section.astro';
---

<Section tone="pearl" labelledby="setup-title">
  <div class="heading">
    <p class="text-label-m label">The setup</p>
    <h2 id="setup-title">
      A plan built from what was clear, <span class="muted">not a guess at the whole</span>
    </h2>
  </div>
  <p class="text-body-xl lead">
    Before Pearl had a single token, the client wanted to know when it would be done. It was a
    fair question, but there was no honest answer yet. I’d usually audit the wireframes first to
    see which components the product actually needs, and here the wireframes were still being
    drawn. So instead of guessing at the whole system, I committed to the parts I could see
    clearly, the foundations and the atomic components the early wireframes already showed. I
    estimated them in hours rather than days, which made every step easy to track, and the rest of
    the system would take shape as the wireframes did.
  </p>
</Section>

<style>
  .heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  .label {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  h2 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .muted {
    color: var(--text-light);
  }

  .lead {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Mobile: 24 between the headline and the text, the same in every section (user). */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .lead {
      margin-top: var(--space-24);
    }
  }
</style>
